# v2.3.2330: cache headers for Cloudflare Pages.  Vite copies public/ into
# dist/ verbatim, which is where Pages reads this from; there was no _headers
# file anywhere before, so every one of the ~700 assets on a repeat load was
# revalidated -- bytes saved, round trips not.
#
# ONLY the content-hashed tree.  /assets/* filenames carry a build hash, so a
# changed file is a new URL and "immutable" can never serve a stale one.  The
# sprite and audio trees are NOT here: many of their URLs are cache-busted by a
# ?v= that the code appends, but not all of them are, and a year of immutable
# on a file that quietly changes is the "it looks fine for me" bug.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# v2.3.2959: the Wheel's ground pictures (public/world/ground/).  The owner's
# phone fell behind walking the Wheel on a slow connection: every tile was
# revalidated, a round trip each, every visit.  The worker asks for each at
# ?v=<its manifest's date>, so a new upload is a new address and keeping the
# old one forever is safe; the manifest itself is fetched at a fresh address
# every time (public/tools/world/core/ground-worker.js).
/world/ground/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# v2.3.3136: the farm's pictures (public/world/farm/), the owner's.  The game
# asks for each at ?v=<FARM_ART_V> (src/data/farmArt.js, written by
# tools/world/add-farm-art.mjs with every run), so a new cut is a new address.
# Nothing in the game fetches manifest.json; whatever does must ask at a fresh
# address, as the ground's worker does.
/world/farm/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
